skill: Power BI

@ Power BI Basics | B
What is Power BI Desktop mainly used for?
= Building data models and reports
- Hosting websites
- Writing mobile apps
- Running a database server
? Power BI Desktop is the authoring tool where you connect to data, model it and design reports.

@ Power BI Basics | I
Which tool in Power BI is used to clean and transform data before loading it?
= Power Query Editor
- The report canvas
- Q&A visual
- The Format pane
? Power Query lets you remove columns, change types, merge tables and filter rows before the data is loaded.

@ Power BI Basics | I
Which Power BI service feature refreshes a dataset automatically at set times?
= Scheduled refresh
- Bookmarks
- Drill-through
- Export to PDF
? Scheduled refresh keeps published reports current without manual action.

@ DAX | B
Which language is used to write measures and calculated columns in Power BI?
= DAX
- VBA
- HTML
- Java
? DAX (Data Analysis Expressions) is the formula language for Power BI data models.

@ DAX | I
Which DAX expression defines a measure for total sales?
= Total Sales = SUM(Sales[Amount])
- Total Sales = ADD(Sales.Amount)
- SELECT SUM(Amount) FROM Sales
- Total Sales := TOTAL Sales[Amount]
? SUM takes a column reference in the form Table[Column].

@ DAX | A
What does the CALCULATE function do in DAX?
= Evaluates an expression in a modified filter context
- Creates a new table from a file
- Deletes rows from a table
- Formats a number as currency
? CALCULATE changes the filters applied to an expression, which is the basis of most advanced measures.

@ DAX | A
What is the main difference between a calculated column and a measure?
= A calculated column is computed per row and stored, while a measure is computed at query time using the filter context
- A measure is stored per row and a column is computed at query time
- They are the same thing
- Measures can only be used in Power Query
? Measures respond to slicers and filters in the report, while calculated columns are fixed at refresh.

@ Data Modeling | I
Which relationship is the most common between a dimension table and a fact table?
= One-to-many
- Many-to-many
- One-to-one
- No relationship
? One row in the dimension table (for example one product) relates to many rows in the fact table (many sales).

@ Visuals | I
Which visual is best for showing parts of a whole when there are only a few categories?
= Donut chart
- Scatter plot
- Line chart
- Matrix with no totals
? Pie and donut charts show proportions and work best with a small number of slices.

@ Visuals | B
What does a slicer do in a Power BI report?
= Lets users filter the other visuals on the page
- Splits a table into files
- Deletes selected rows
- Creates a new measure
? A slicer is an on-canvas filter that users can click to change what other visuals show.
